      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/SkeneTechnologies/skene\n\n### Category\n\nPython\n\n### Project Title\n\nA codebase analysis toolkit that finds product-led growth opportunities and generates implementation plans.\n\n### Project Description\n\nSkene scans your codebase to detect the technology stack, existing growth features, and revenue leakage, then produces recommendations with ready-to-use implementation prompts for AI coding tools like Cursor and Claude. Works with OpenAI, Gemini, Claude, Ollama, LM Studio, and any OpenAI-compatible LLM provider.\n\n### Highlights\n\n - Interactive terminal interface\n - Free local audit mode, no API key required\n - Auto-detects frameworks, databases, auth, signup flows, sharing, invites, and billing\n - Generates implementation prompts ready to drop into Cursor, Claude, or other AI coding tools\n - Supports OpenAI, Gemini, Claude, LM Studio, Ollama, and any OpenAI-compatible endpoint\n - Tracks features across runs and validates whether growth feature requirements are implemented\n\n### Example Code\n\n```markdown\n# Install the terminal user interface and launch the wizard\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SkeneTechnologies/skene/main/tui/install.sh | bash skene\n\n# Or run the Python CLI directly without installing\nuvx skene\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/49dcd0c4-2bad-4fd3-b29e-89ba2b85c669",
